"\u002Fplatform\u002Fsupply-chain-security","02.platform\u002F14.supply-chain-security","i-lucide-package-check",{"title":233,"path":234,"stem":235,"icon":236},"Enterprise License","\u002Fplatform\u002Fenterprise-license","02.platform\u002F15.enterprise-license","i-lucide-badge-check",{"id":238,"title":153,"body":239,"description":666,"extension":667,"links":668,"meta":669,"navigation":670,"path":154,"seo":671,"stem":155,"__hash__":672},"docs\u002F02.platform\u002F02.deployment-guide.md",{"type":240,"value":241,"toc":654},"minimark",[242,247,251,255,259,264,272,302,305,431,461,472,476,487,490,495,499,506,520,525,574,599,617,638],[243,244,246],"alert",{"type":245},"info","Detailed deployment guide coming soon.",[248,249,25],"h2",{"id":250},"overview",[252,253,254],"p",{},"Kinotic OS deploys to Kubernetes and provides several deployment configurations for different environments.",[248,256,258],{"id":257},"deployment-options","Deployment Options",[260,261,263],"h3",{"id":262},"helm-charts","Helm Charts",[252,265,266,267,271],{},"Production-ready Helm charts are available in ",[268,269,270],"code",{},"deployment\u002Fhelm\u002F"," for deploying:",[273,274,275,290,296],"ul",{},[276,277,278,282,283,286,287],"li",{},[279,280,281],"strong",{},"Kinotic servers"," — ",[268,284,285],{},"deployment\u002Fhelm\u002Fkinotic",": the org, system and app servers in one release, each a Deployment, Service and ConfigMap of its own with its replicas, resources, service type and TLS certificate, and the migration Job that precedes them. Every server's pods join one headless Service, through which Ignite discovers its peers, so the three form one cluster, and each server signs tokens with a JWT key set of its own, ",[268,288,289],{},"\u003Cserver>-jwt-signing-keys",[276,291,292,295],{},[279,293,294],{},"Elasticsearch"," — Search and persistence cluster",[276,297,298,301],{},[279,299,300],{},"Load Generator"," — For performance testing",[252,303,304],{},"Each server mounts a system-secrets volume, projected from the global Key Vault. It holds the server's JWT key set and the\nsecrets the server imports as properties when it starts, each file named after the property it\nsets:",[306,307,308,324],"table",{},[309,310,311],"thead",{},[312,313,314,318,321],"tr",{},[315,316,317],"th",{},"File",[315,319,320],{},"Key Vault secret",[315,322,323],{},"Mounted on",[325,326,327,342,357,379,394,412],"tbody",{},[312,328,329,335,339],{},[330,331,332],"td",{},[268,333,334],{},"jwt-signing-keys",[330,336,337],{},[268,338,289],{},[330,340,341],{},"each server, its own key set",[312,343,344,349,354],{},[330,345,346],{},[268,347,348],{},"kinotic.domain.secretStorage.masterKey",[330,350,351],{},[268,352,353],{},"kinotic-secret-storage-master-key",[330,355,356],{},"every server",[312,358,359,364,369],{},[330,360,361],{},[268,362,363],{},"kinotic.managementApi.github.appPrivateKey",[330,365,366],{},[268,367,368],{},"kinotic-github-app-private-key",[330,370,371,372,375,376],{},"the servers with ",[268,373,374],{},"githubApp"," set: the org and system servers, which load ",[268,377,378],{},"management-api",[312,380,381,386,391],{},[330,382,383],{},[268,384,385],{},"kinotic.managementApi.github.webhookSecret",[330,387,388],{},[268,389,390],{},"kinotic-github-webhook-secret",[330,392,393],{},"the same",[312,395,396,401,406],{},[330,397,398],{},[268,399,400],{},"kinotic.domain.publishedSites.cloudflare.apiToken",[330,402,403],{},[268,404,405],{},"kinotic-cloudflare-dns-api-token",[330,407,371,408,411],{},[268,409,410],{},"cloudflareDns"," set: the management and system servers, which create an organization's sites record",[312,413,414,419,424],{},[330,415,416],{},[268,417,418],{},"kinotic.managementServer.turnstile.secretKey",[330,420,421],{},[268,422,423],{},"kinotic-turnstile-secret-key",[330,425,426,427,430],{},"the server with ",[268,428,429],{},"turnstile"," set: the management server, which verifies the find-my-organizations challenge",[252,432,433,436,437,440,441,444,445,448,449,452,453,456,457,460],{},[268,434,435],{},"kinotic.domain.secretStorage.backend"," selects where ",[268,438,439],{},"SecretStorageService"," persists secrets.\n",[268,442,443],{},"IN_MEMORY",", the default, keeps them in process memory, so a restart loses every stored secret. ",[268,446,447],{},"AZURE"," stores them in\nthe Key Vault at ",[268,450,451],{},"kinotic.domain.secretStorage.azure.vaultUrl","; that backend is an Enterprise\nFeature in the ",[268,454,455],{},"kinotic-ee"," module, which the org, system and app servers include, and its\nproduction use needs a Kinotic Enterprise License agreement with Minds Ignited (see\n",[458,459,233],"a",{"href":234},"). A server\nconfigured with a backend whose module is not on its classpath fails at startup.",[252,462,463,464,467,468,471],{},"A server picks up a rotated JWT key set while it runs, and an imported secret when it restarts.\nOn Azure the global terraform seeds the master key and takes the GitHub App's key and webhook\nsecret from ",[268,465,466],{},"TF_VAR_github_app_private_key"," and ",[268,469,470],{},"TF_VAR_github_webhook_secret",".",[260,473,475],{"id":474},"docker-compose-local-development","Docker Compose (Local Development)",[252,477,478,479,482,483,486],{},"A Docker Compose configuration in ",[268,480,481],{},"deployment\u002Fdocker-compose\u002F"," provides a complete local development environment including the org, system and app servers (",[268,484,485],{},"compose.kinotic-servers.yml","), Elasticsearch, and supporting services. This is the recommended way to run Kinotic OS during development.",[260,488,223],{"id":489},"development-server",[252,491,492,493,471],{},"A single-host development environment on Proxmox — a container per service, the three servers\nbehind an edge that routes the one forwarded port by SNI, three Elasticsearch nodes on their own\ndisks, and Cloud Hypervisor nodes on machines of their own — that keeps the sites account and\nemail in Azure, the sites on Cloudflare, and is designed to migrate its organizations to Kinotic Cloud. See\n",[458,494,223],{"href":224},[260,496,498],{"id":497},"cloud-providers-terraform","Cloud Providers (Terraform)",[252,500,501,502,505],{},"Terraform configurations in ",[268,503,504],{},"deployment\u002Fterraform\u002F"," support deployment to:",[273,507,508,514],{},[276,509,510,513],{},[279,511,512],{},"AWS"," — EC2-based deployment with configurable instance types",[276,515,516,519],{},[279,517,518],{},"Azure"," — VM-based deployment on Azure infrastructure",[521,522,524],"h4",{"id":523},"ui-sites-on-cloudflare","UI sites on Cloudflare",[252,526,527,528,531,532,535,536,539,540,543,544,547,548,535,551,554,555,467,558,561,562,565,566,569,570,573],{},"Published UIs live on the customer domain, a Cloudflare zone (",[268,529,530],{},"kinotic.io",") separate from\nthe platform's own, so that no customer content is ever under the domain the portal's cookies\nlive on. ",[268,533,534],{},"sites.tf"," calls ",[268,537,538],{},"deployment\u002Fterraform\u002Fazure\u002Fmodules\u002Fsites"," for the sites storage\naccount ",[268,541,542],{},"st\u003Cprefix>sites"," every site's files live in under ",[268,545,546],{},"sites\u002F\u003Chostname>\u002F",", private, with\na read-only SAS on its container minted for the edge; ",[268,549,550],{},"cloudflare.tf",[268,552,553],{},"modules\u002Fcloudflare-sites"," for the edge,\nonce per environment: the zone's settings (Full (strict), HTTPS only, TLS 1.2) and Total TLS,\nthe proxied records ",[268,556,557],{},"apps-api.\u003Czone>",[268,559,560],{},"*.apps-api.\u003Czone>"," to the app server's load\nbalancer, and the sites Worker (",[268,563,564],{},"deployment\u002Fcloudflare\u002Fsites-worker",") bound to ",[268,567,568],{},"*.\u003Czone>\u002F*",",\nwith the apps-api hosts bound to no Worker so API calls and WebSockets reach the app server\ndirectly. A site is ",[268,571,572],{},"\u003Capp>--\u003Cui>.\u003Corg>.\u003Czone>","; the Worker reads it from the account and\nserves a route of the single-page application its index. Nothing is created per application,\nUI or tenant.",[252,575,576,577,580,581,584,585,588,589,591,592,594,595,598],{},"Per organization, two proxied records are created, and the platform creates them: the wildcard\n",[268,578,579],{},"*.\u003Corg>.\u003Czone>"," for its sites and ",[268,582,583],{},"\u003Corg>.\u003Czone>"," for its own host, at sign-up (the management server)\nor before the organization's first publish (the system server), through ",[268,586,587],{},"CloudflareOrganizationDnsRecordProvisioner"," with a token holding\nDNS edit on the zone and nothing else, which the global root stores in the platform vault as\n",[268,590,405],{},". Total TLS issues the organization's certificate from the\nrecord within minutes, and ",[268,593,583],{}," itself, covered by the zone's universal\ncertificate, redirects to the portal's login for the organization. The app server's names in\nthe zone are on the cluster certificate: cert-manager answers their DNS-01 challenges through\nCloudflare with the same token (",[268,596,597],{},"tls.tf","), so Full (strict) validates the origin.",[252,600,601,602,604,605,608,609,612,613,616],{},"The portal's find-my-organizations form presents a Cloudflare Turnstile challenge, and the\nmanagement server verifies each request's token: the global root stores the site's secret key in the\nplatform vault as ",[268,603,423],{}," (",[268,606,607],{},"TF_VAR_turnstile_secret_key","), and the cluster\nroot passes the site key as ",[268,610,611],{},"turnstile_site_key",", which Helm hands the management server as\n",[268,614,615],{},"kinotic.managementServer.turnstile.siteKey",". The site is created in the Cloudflare dashboard under\nTurnstile, for the portal's hostname.",[252,618,619,622,623,626,627,629,630,633,634,637],{},[268,620,621],{},"kinotic.tf"," passes the zone as the sites domain and the account's blob endpoint to the system\nserver as ",[268,624,625],{},"KINOTIC_SYSTEMAPI_UIDEPLOYMENT_*",", the app server's ",[268,628,557],{}," base, and the\n",[268,631,632],{},"KINOTIC_DOMAIN_PUBLISHEDSITES_*"," settings every server provisions organizations with (see\n",[458,635,157],{"href":636},"\u002Fplatform\u002Fconfiguration#ui-sites","). The cluster root takes the zone's id, the\naccount id and two tokens as variables: the operator's, which terraform applies the zone and\nthe Worker with, and the DNS token. The system server's development profile disables the\nprovisioner instead.",[252,639,640,641,644,645,648,649,653],{},"A developer machine gets the same modules from ",[268,642,643],{},"deployment\u002Fterraform\u002Fazure\u002Fdev",", under\n",[268,646,647],{},"\u003Cenvironment>.\u003Czone>",". The ",[458,650,652],{"href":651},"\u002Fplatform\u002Fcontributing#publishing-uis-against-azure","contributing guide","\nwalks through it.",{"title":655,"searchDepth":656,"depth":656,"links":657},"",2,[658,659],{"id":250,"depth":656,"text":25},{"id":257,"depth":656,"text":258,"children":660},[661,663,664,665],{"id":262,"depth":662,"text":263},3,{"id":474,"depth":662,"text":475},{"id":489,"depth":662,"text":223},{"id":497,"depth":662,"text":498},"Deploying and operating Kinotic OS in various environments.","md",null,{},{"icon":6},{"title":153,"description":666},"aTZqApIF3NxuiyzX10VcR9p-M_aHV8xrOyMbkVFJa0Y",[674,676],{"title":148,"path":149,"stem":150,"description":675,"icon":151,"children":-1},"High-level architecture of the Kinotic OS platform.",{"title":157,"path":158,"stem":159,"description":677,"icon":160,"children":-1},"Configuration reference for Kinotic OS server and services.",1792907302573]